      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would like to say that fundamental problem of why this abuse is possible - **most users just know nothing** about group instances and **can't easily split apart** \"free\" instances and \"managed\" instances.\n\nFirst of all, group publics **looks almost the same** as normal publics.\n\nGroup name looks the same as username, and no one checks usernames with no need.\n\nAlso, \"3-dots\" and \"crown\" icons **have no obvious meaning**. When groups just were introduced, all my friends who not watching development was \"wtf is these 3 dots in main menu?\" It's just **not clear for users** who not familiar with how instances work. (This also related to \"locked\" and \"unlocked\" instances, a lot of users know nothing about this, but this is kind of different story.)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
